.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-APPS 1
.Os Wattle 0.2.2
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-apps
.Nd manage installed applications
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "wattle apps"
.Ar verb
.Oo
.Ar argument
.Oc
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "wattle apps"
manages installed applications.
An
.Em application
is a project with executable programs for installation.
See
.Xr wattle-applications 7
for the application layout and installation requirements.
.Pp
Each application is installed in
.Eo
.Pa lib/wattle/apps/<group>/<name>/
.Ec
under
.Ql "*prefix*" .
Programs are installed in
.Eo
.Pa bin/
.Ec
and manual pages in
.Eo
.Pa share/man/
.Ec .
An application’s modules are not made available for import
by other applications.
.Pp
A build made without the OS library does not include
.Cm apps .
Each verb reports this limitation and exits with status 1.
.Ic a
is a synonym for
.Cm apps .
.
.Sh VERBS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Cm install
.Oo
.Ar source
.Oo
.Ar ref
.Oc
.Oc
.Xc
Install an application.
.Ar source
is a directory,
a name ending in
.Ql "\&.tar"
or
.Ql "\&.tar\&.gz" ,
or a Git repository.
A directory is installed as it is.
A name ending in
.Ql "\&.tar"
or
.Ql "\&.tar\&.gz"
is downloaded with
.Ic curl
and unpacked with
.Ic tar .
Anything else is cloned with
.Ic git .
With no
.Ar source ,
the current directory is installed.
The application’s info file requires
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":group" .
The group is conventionally a reverse domain such as
.Ql "net\&.inqk" .
Installed application names are unique across groups.
.Pp
The project declares the programs to install under
.Ql ":exes" .
Native executables are built and installed in
.Eo
.Pa bin/
.Ec .
Source executables are copied with a program in
.Eo
.Pa bin/
.Ec
that runs them.
Associated libraries and manual pages are installed with the
programs.
Web executables are not installed.
An application script,
if present,
replaces this installation with custom hooks.
See
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
.Pp
.Ar ref
specifies a branch or tag and applies only to a Git repository.
.It Xo
.Cm upgrade
.Oo
.Ar name
.Oc
.Xc
Install the application
.Ar name
again from the source it was installed from.
An application installed from a tarball or a Git repository
is downloaded again.
With no
.Ar name ,
every installed application is upgraded.
.It Xo
.Cm remove
.Ar name
.Xc
Remove the application
.Ar name .
.It Xo
.Cm list
.Xc
List the installed applications.
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Install applications from a directory,
a tarball and a Git repository,
and list the installed applications:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle apps install \&./my-app
$ wattle apps install https://example\&.com/my-app\&.tar\&.gz
$ wattle apps install https://example\&.com/my-app\&.git v1\&.2
$ wattle apps list
.Ed
.Pp
Install every application again from its source,
and remove one:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle apps upgrade
$ wattle apps remove my-app
.Ed
.
